IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-2-explanations`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`
IMPORT `chapter-17-property`

§ `Chapter 17 -- Aggravated theft, extortion, robbery and gang-robbery`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 380, 381, 382, 383, 385, 386, 387, 388, 389, 390, 391, 393,
-- 394, 396, 397, 399, 400, 401, 402.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Shape of the group. ss 380 to 382 are theft (s 378, already encoded) plus one
-- aggravating circumstance. s 383 defines extortion, and ss 385 to 389 are either
-- extortion by a particular kind of fear or the attempt to induce that fear. s 390 is
-- the hinge: "In all robbery there is either theft or extortion", and it gives two
-- separate tests for when each becomes robbery. ss 391 to 402 build on robbery.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED. ss 379, 379A, 384, 392 and 395 are punishment sections
-- and are not encoded. ss 393, 394, 396 and 397 are encoded despite being framed as
-- punishment provisions, because each states a distinct combination of facts a caller
-- may want to test -- the same treatment ss 323A and 375(3) get in Chapter 16.

§§ `Sections 380, 381 and 382 -- Aggravated theft`

-- Each is s 378 theft plus a circumstance: committed in a dwelling or place of
-- custody (s 380); committed by a clerk or servant against the master's property
-- (s 381); or committed after preparation for causing death, hurt or restraint, in
-- order to commit it, to escape after it, or to retain what was taken (s 382).
-- The s 382 Illustrations are both cases of carrying a weapon provided in advance
-- against the possibility of resistance.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 380"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes theft in a dwelling house under Penal Code 1871 section 380
GIVEN t IS A `Property Taking` @desc The s 378 taking facts, where the theft was committed in a building, tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. Theft requires that the taking be dishonest under s 24.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes theft in a dwelling house` t f IF
        `constitutes theft` t f
    AND t's `the theft is committed in a building tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 381"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes theft by a clerk or servant under Penal Code 1871 section 381
GIVEN t IS A `Property Taking` @desc The s 378 taking facts, where the accused is a clerk or servant and the property is in the possession of his master or employer.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements for theft.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes theft by a clerk or servant` t f IF
        `constitutes theft` t f
    AND t's `the accused is a clerk or servant or employed in the capacity of a clerk or servant and the property is in the possession of his master or employer`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 382"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes theft after preparation for causing death or hurt under Penal Code 1871 section 382
GIVEN t IS A `Property Taking` @desc The s 378 taking facts, where preparation was made for causing death, hurt or restraint in order to commit the theft, to escape after it, or to retain the property.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements for theft.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes theft after preparation for causing hurt` t f IF
        `constitutes theft` t f
    AND t's `having made preparation for causing death hurt or restraint or fear of death hurt or restraint to any person in order to commit the theft or to effect escape after it or to retain property taken by it`

§§ `Section 383 -- Extortion`

-- Whoever intentionally puts any person in fear of any harm to that person or to any
-- other person, in body, mind, reputation or property, whether the harm is to be
-- caused legally or illegally, and thereby dishonestly induces the person so put in
-- fear to deliver to any person any property or valuable security, or anything signed
-- or sealed which may be converted into a valuable security.
--
-- Two elements only: the intentional putting in fear, and the delivery dishonestly
-- induced by it. Note "whether such harm is to be caused legally or illegally" --
-- threatening to do something one is entitled to do is still extortion if it induces
-- the delivery. Illustration (c) is that case: a threat to report a real offence.
-- Illustration (d) is why the last limb matters: a signed blank paper capable of
-- being converted into a valuable security is enough.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 383"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes extortion under Penal Code 1871 section 383
GIVEN e IS AN Extortion @desc Intentionally putting a person in fear of harm, and thereby dishonestly inducing delivery of property, a valuable security, or anything signed or sealed convertible into one.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes extortion` IF
        e's `intentionally puts any person in fear of any harm to that person or to any other person in body mind reputation or property whether the harm is to be caused legally or illegally`
    AND e's `thereby dishonestly induces the person so put in fear to deliver to any person any property or valuable security or anything signed or sealed which may be converted into a valuable security`

§§ `Sections 385 to 389 -- Aggravated extortion, and putting in fear to commit it`

-- The five sections pair off. ss 386 and 388 are extortion *committed* by a
-- particular kind of fear; ss 385, 387 and 389 are putting or attempting to put a
-- person in fear *in order to* commit extortion, which needs no delivery at all.
--
--   s 385  putting in fear of any harm, in order to commit extortion
--   s 386  extortion by fear of death or grievous hurt
--   s 387  putting in fear of death or grievous hurt, in order to commit extortion
--   s 388  extortion by fear of an accusation of a serious offence
--   s 389  putting in fear of such an accusation, in order to commit extortion
--
-- s 388 has a limb s 389 lacks: fear of an accusation of having *attempted to induce
-- another* to commit such an offence. It is encoded on s 388 only.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 385"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes putting a person in fear of harm in order to commit extortion under Penal Code 1871 section 385
GIVEN e IS AN Extortion @desc Putting or attempting to put a person in fear of harm, in order to commit extortion. No delivery need follow.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes putting in fear to commit extortion` IF
        e's `in order to commit extortion puts or attempts to put any person in fear`
    AND e's `intentionally puts any person in fear of any harm to that person or to any other person in body mind reputation or property whether the harm is to be caused legally or illegally`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 386"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes extortion by putting a person in fear of death or grievous hurt under Penal Code 1871 section 386
GIVEN e IS AN Extortion @desc Extortion committed by putting a person in fear of death or of grievous hurt.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes extortion by fear of death or grievous hurt` IF
        `constitutes extortion` e
    AND e's `the fear is of death or of grievous hurt to that person or to any other`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 387"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes putting a person in fear of death or grievous hurt in order to commit extortion under Penal Code 1871 section 387
GIVEN e IS AN Extortion @desc Putting or attempting to put a person in fear of death or grievous hurt, in order to commit extortion.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes putting in fear of death to commit extortion` IF
        e's `in order to commit extortion puts or attempts to put any person in fear`
    AND e's `the fear is of death or of grievous hurt to that person or to any other`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 388"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes extortion by threat of accusation of a serious offence under Penal Code 1871 section 388
GIVEN e IS AN Extortion @desc Extortion committed by putting a person in fear of an accusation of an offence punishable with death, imprisonment for life or imprisonment up to 10 years, or of having attempted to induce another to commit one.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes extortion by threat of accusation` IF
        `constitutes extortion` e
    AND (   e's `the fear is of an accusation against that person or any other of having committed or attempted to commit an offence punishable with death with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 10 years`
         OR e's `the fear is of an accusation of having attempted to induce any other person to commit such an offence`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 389"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes putting a person in fear of an accusation in order to commit extortion under Penal Code 1871 section 389
GIVEN e IS AN Extortion @desc Putting or attempting to put a person in fear of an accusation of a serious offence, in order to commit extortion. Unlike s 388 this section does not extend to an accusation of attempting to induce another.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes putting in fear of accusation to commit extortion` IF
        e's `in order to commit extortion puts or attempts to put any person in fear`
    AND e's `the fear is of an accusation against that person or any other of having committed or attempted to commit an offence punishable with death with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 10 years`

§§ `Section 390 -- Robbery`

-- s 390(1): "In all robbery there is either theft or extortion." The two routes are
-- genuinely different and the section gives each its own test.
--
-- s 390(2), theft: the offender, in order to commit the theft, in committing it, or
-- in carrying away or attempting to carry away the property, and FOR THAT END,
-- voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death, hurt or wrongful restraint, or fear
-- of any of them instantly. Illustration (a) is holding a person down while taking
-- his money.
--
-- s 390(3), extortion: the offender is in the presence of the person put in fear,
-- commits the extortion by fear of INSTANT death, hurt or wrongful restraint, and by
-- so putting in fear induces delivery THEN AND THERE. The Explanation defines
-- presence as being sufficiently near to put the person in fear of the instant harm.
-- Illustration (d) is the case that fails: a threat to kill a child held elsewhere by
-- the offender's gang is extortion, and is not robbery, because the fear is not of
-- instant death.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 390(2)"
GIVEN r IS A Robbery
      t IS A `Property Taking`
      f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the theft is robbery` r t f IF
        `constitutes theft` t f
    AND r's `in order to commit the theft or in committing it or in carrying away or attempting to carry away property obtained by it`
    AND r's `for that end voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to any person death hurt or wrongful restraint or fear of instant death instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 390(3)"
GIVEN r IS A Robbery
      e IS AN Extortion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the extortion is robbery` r e IF
        `constitutes extortion` e
    AND r's `at the time of committing the extortion the offender is in the presence of the person put in fear`
    AND r's `commits the extortion by putting that person in fear of instant death instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint to that person or to some other person`
    AND r's `by so putting in fear induces the person then and there to deliver up the thing extorted`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 390"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes robbery under Penal Code 1871 section 390
GIVEN r IS A Robbery @desc The robbery facts. In all robbery there is either theft or extortion, and each has its own test in s 390(2) and s 390(3).
      t IS A `Property Taking` @desc The s 378 taking facts, for the theft route.
      e IS AN Extortion @desc The s 383 facts, for the extortion route.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements for theft.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes robbery` r t e f IF
        `the theft is robbery` r t f
    OR  `the extortion is robbery` r e

§§ `Section 391 -- Gang-robbery`

-- When 5 or more persons conjointly commit or attempt to commit a robbery, or where
-- the whole number of those committing or attempting it together with those present
-- and aiding amounts to 5 or more, every one of them commits gang-robbery.
-- Note that the count includes those merely present and aiding, and that an ATTEMPT
-- at robbery is enough -- so gang-robbery does not require `constitutes robbery` to
-- be made out, only the robbery or the attempt at it.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 391"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes gang-robbery under Penal Code 1871 section 391
GIVEN r IS A Robbery @desc Five or more persons conjointly committing or attempting the robbery, counting those present and aiding.
      t IS A `Property Taking` @desc The s 378 taking facts.
      e IS AN Extortion @desc The s 383 facts.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements for theft.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes gang-robbery` r t e f IF
        (   `constitutes robbery` r t e f
         OR r's `attempts to commit robbery`)
    AND r's `5 or more persons conjointly commit or attempt to commit the robbery or the persons so committing or attempting together with those present and aiding amount to 5 or more`

§§ `Sections 393, 394, 396 and 397 -- The aggravated robberies`

-- s 393: attempting to commit robbery.
-- s 394: hurt voluntarily caused in committing or attempting robbery -- and note the
-- section reaches "any other person jointly concerned", so joint concern is an
-- alternative route into it and not a further requirement on the person who caused
-- the hurt.
-- s 396: gang-robbery where any one of the 5 or more commits murder in so doing.
-- s 397: robbery where the offender is armed with or uses a deadly weapon, or causes
-- grievous hurt, or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt -- again extended to
-- any person jointly concerned.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 393"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes an attempt to commit robbery under Penal Code 1871 section 393
GIVEN r IS A Robbery @desc An attempt to commit robbery.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes attempted robbery` IF
    r's `attempts to commit robbery`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 394"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes voluntarily causing hurt in committing robbery under Penal Code 1871 section 394
GIVEN r IS A Robbery @desc Hurt voluntarily caused in committing or attempting robbery, by the offender or by a person jointly concerned.
      t IS A `Property Taking` @desc The s 378 taking facts.
      e IS AN Extortion @desc The s 383 facts.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements for theft.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes causing hurt in robbery` r t e f IF
        (   `constitutes robbery` r t e f
         OR r's `attempts to commit robbery`)
    AND r's `in committing or attempting to commit the robbery voluntarily causes hurt`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 396"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes gang-robbery with murder under Penal Code 1871 section 396
GIVEN r IS A Robbery @desc Gang-robbery where one of the 5 or more persons commits murder in so committing it.
      t IS A `Property Taking` @desc The s 378 taking facts.
      e IS AN Extortion @desc The s 383 facts.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements for theft.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes gang-robbery with murder` r t e f IF
        `constitutes gang-robbery` r t e f
    AND r's `one of the 5 or more persons conjointly committing the gang-robbery commits murder in so committing it`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 397"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes robbery when armed or with attempt to cause death or grievous hurt under Penal Code 1871 section 397
GIVEN r IS A Robbery @desc Robbery or attempted robbery where the offender is armed with or uses a deadly weapon, or causes grievous hurt, or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt.
      t IS A `Property Taking` @desc The s 378 taking facts.
      e IS AN Extortion @desc The s 383 facts.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements for theft.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes armed or deadly robbery` r t e f IF
        (   `constitutes robbery` r t e f
         OR r's `attempts to commit robbery`)
    AND (   r's `at the time of committing or attempting to commit the robbery the offender is armed with or uses any deadly weapon`
         OR r's `at that time the offender causes grievous hurt to any person or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person`)

§§ `Sections 399 to 402 -- Preparation, gangs and assembly`

-- These four punish conduct short of any robbery, and none of them requires one:
-- s 399 preparation for gang-robbery; s 400 belonging to a gang associated for
-- habitually committing gang-robbery; s 401 belonging to a gang associated for
-- habitually committing theft or robbery and NOT being gang-robbers -- which is why
-- the two sections are mutually exclusive on their face; s 402 being one of 5 or
-- more assembled for the purpose of committing gang-robbery.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 399"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes making preparation to commit gang-robbery under Penal Code 1871 section 399
GIVEN r IS A Robbery @desc Preparation made for committing gang-robbery. No robbery need follow.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes preparation for gang-robbery` IF
    r's `makes any preparation for committing gang-robbery`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 400"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes belonging to a gang of gang-robbers under Penal Code 1871 section 400
GIVEN r IS A Robbery @desc Belonging to a gang associated for the purpose of habitually committing gang-robbery.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes belonging to a gang of gang-robbers` IF
    r's `belongs to a gang of persons associated for the purpose of habitually committing gang-robbery`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 401"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes belonging to a gang of thieves under Penal Code 1871 section 401
GIVEN r IS A Robbery @desc Belonging to a gang associated for habitually committing theft or robbery, and not being gang-robbers. The section is mutually exclusive with s 400 on its face.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes belonging to a gang of thieves` IF
    r's `belongs to a gang of persons associated for the purpose of habitually committing theft or robbery and not being gang-robbers`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 402"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes assembling for the purpose of committing gang-robbery under Penal Code 1871 section 402
GIVEN r IS A Robbery @desc Being one of 5 or more persons assembled for the purpose of committing gang-robbery.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes assembling for gang-robbery` IF
    r's `is one of 5 or more persons assembled for the purpose of committing gang-robbery`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes aggravated theft` IF
        (   `constitutes theft in a dwelling house` (a's `property taking`) (a's `fault`)
         OR `constitutes theft by a clerk or servant` (a's `property taking`) (a's `fault`)
         OR `constitutes theft after preparation for causing hurt` (a's `property taking`) (a's `fault`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes extortion` IF
        (   `constitutes extortion` (a's `extortion`)
         OR `constitutes putting in fear to commit extortion` (a's `extortion`)
         OR `constitutes putting in fear of death to commit extortion` (a's `extortion`)
         OR `constitutes putting in fear of accusation to commit extortion` (a's `extortion`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes robbery` IF
        `constitutes robbery` (a's `robbery`) (a's `property taking`) (a's `extortion`) (a's `fault`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes gang-robbery` IF
        `constitutes gang-robbery` (a's `robbery`) (a's `property taking`) (a's `extortion`) (a's `fault`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a gang-robbery preparatory offence` IF
        (   `constitutes preparation for gang-robbery` (a's `robbery`)
         OR `constitutes belonging to a gang of gang-robbers` (a's `robbery`)
         OR `constitutes belonging to a gang of thieves` (a's `robbery`)
         OR `constitutes assembling for gang-robbery` (a's `robbery`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
